  "rhythm": "Songsterr s454550 bars 38-41 (4/4, 143 BPM; Hooktheory and the bitmidi MIDI both say 143): the chorus's closing line from its downbeat, then the tag, note values straight from the vocal track; the singer never stops for half a beat here, so there are no rests. Hooktheory's chorus has the same notes and rhythm; it ends the tag's second half on F# where Songsterr holds G4, and G4 (the fifth of C minor, the phrase's last syllable) is kept as the ending. Real tempo, no slow-down: the shortest note is an eighth (0.21 s). No simplification on the ocarina. The string riff's sixteenths are too fast for the ocarina at 143, so the ocarina keeps the vocal and the riff plays at full speed in the strings part. Drums: 2 bars of intro (bars 36-37) and the tab's drum machine pattern (kick 1 and the and of 2, snare 2 and 4, shaker and cymbal on every beat; the tab's crash-2 quarters are a softer ride here) plus quiet sixteenth hats so every part's onsets land on a hit. Parts (all at the melody's shift, 0): bass from the finger bass (intro at pitch, song an octave up), strings riff (upper octave of the tab's octave pairs), clean twang guitar an octave down on sitar, rhythm acoustic chords on nylon guitar, distorted guitar stabs on trombone (bar 41 an octave down). Learned 2026-09-30 for cratervale. 2026-09-30 mix (Poodleskirt 'no ocarina? lol', vorime 'totally overpowered'): the rhythm acoustic chords (168 notes) left out, strings 84->66, sitar 74->52, trombone 72->52, bass 100->84, so the ocarina's vocal line sits on top.",
